# VLM Run MCP API - Function Reference

This document provides a comprehensive overview of the VLM Run MCP API functions.

## Table of Contents
- [File Management](#file-management)
- [OpenAI Compatible Interface](#openai-compatible-interface)
- [Hub Information](#hub-information)
- [Media Processing](#media-processing)
- [Fine-tuning](#fine-tuning)
- [System Information](#system-information)

## File Management

### `get_files_v1_files_get`
Get all files uploaded by the user with pagination.
```
{
  queryParameters: {
    skip: 0,      // Number of items to skip
    limit: 10     // Maximum number of items to return (max: 1000)
  }
}
```

### `upload_file_v1_files_post`
Upload a file.
```
{
  queryParameters: {
    purpose: "assistants"  // Purpose: "assistants", "batch", "fine-tune", "vision", "datasets"
  },
  requestBody: {}
}
```

### `get_file_v1_files_file_id_get`
Get a file by ID.
```
{
  urlParameters: {
    file_id: "file_id_here"  // Required: ID of the file to retrieve
  }
}
```

### `get_file_by_hash_v1_files_hash_file_hash_get`
Check if a file exists by its md5 hash.
```
{
  urlParameters: {
    file_hash: "md5_hash_here"  // Required: MD5 hash of the file
  }
}
```

## OpenAI Compatible Interface

### `health_v1_openai_health_get`
Health check for the OpenAI-compatible API.

### `chat_completions_v1_openai_chat_completions_post`
Chat Completions.
```
{
  requestBody: {
    model: "vlm-1",                      // Default model
    messages: [                          // Required
      {
        role: "user",                    // "user", "assistant", or "system"
        content: "Hello, how are you?"   // String or array of message content
      }
    ],
    max_tokens: 1024,                    // Default: 1024
    temperature: 0.7,                    // Default: 0.7
    top_p: 1,                            // Default: 1
    stream: false                        // Default: false
    // Additional parameters available
  }
}
```

### `models_v1_openai_models_get`
List all available models.

### `model_info_v1_openai_models_model_get`
Get model information.
```
{
  urlParameters: {
    model: "model_name_here"  // Required: Name of the model
  }
}
```

## Hub Information

### `info_v1_hub_info_get`
Get information about the hub.

### `list_domains_v1_hub_domains_get`
Get the list of supported domains.

### `get_domain_schema_v1_hub_schema_post`
Get the JSON schema for a given domain.
```
{
  requestBody: {
    domain: "document.invoice",  // Required: Domain identifier
    gql_stmt: null               // Optional: GraphQL statement
  }
}
```

## Media Processing

### `image_generate_v1_image_generate_post`
Generate structured prediction for the given image.
```
{
  requestBody: {
    images: ["base64_encoded_image_or_url"],  // Required: List of images
    domain: "image.caption",                  // Required: Domain identifier
    model: "vlm-1",                           // Default: "vlm-1"
    batch: false,                             // Default: false (process synchronously)
    config: {
      temperature: 0,                         // Default: 0
      max_tokens: 4096                        // Default: 4096
      // Additional configuration options available
    }
  }
}
```

### `document_generate_v1_document_generate_post`
Generate structured prediction for the given document.
```
{
  requestBody: {
    domain: "document.invoice",  // Required: Domain identifier
    file_id: "file_id_here",     // File ID (provide either file_id or url)
    url: "document_url",         // URL to document (provide either file_id or url)
    batch: true,                 // Default: true (process asynchronously)
    model: "vlm-1",              // Default: "vlm-1"
    config: {
      // Configuration options
    }
  }
}
```

## Fine-tuning

### `health_v1_fine_tuning_health_get`
Health check for the fine-tuning service.

### `list_jobs_v1_fine_tuning_jobs_get`
List fine-tuning jobs.
```
{
  queryParameters: {
    skip: 0,      // Number of items to skip
    limit: 10     // Maximum number of items to return
  }
}
```

### `get_job_v1_fine_tuning_jobs_job_id_get`
Get information about a fine-tuning job.
```
{
  urlParameters: {
    job_id: "job_id_here"  // Required: ID of the job to retrieve
  }
}
```

### `create_job_v1_fine_tuning_create_post`
Create a new fine-tuning job.
```
{
  requestBody: {
    model: "base_model_name",          // Required: Model to fine-tune
    training_file: "file_id_or_url",   // Required: Training dataset
    validation_file: "file_id_or_url", // Optional: Validation dataset
    num_epochs: 8,                     // Default: 8
    batch_size: 8,                     // Default: 8 (can be "auto")
    learning_rate: 0.0002              // Default: 0.0002
    // Additional parameters available
  }
}
```

### `provision_v1_fine_tuning_provision_post`
Provision a new fine-tuned model for inference.
```
{
  requestBody: {
    model: "fine_tuned_model_name",  // Required: Model to provision
    duration: 600,                   // Default: 600 seconds (10 minutes)
    concurrency: 2                   // Default: 2 concurrent requests
  }
}
```

### `generate_v1_fine_tuning_generate_post`
Generate a response from a fine-tuned model.
```
{
  requestBody: {
    model: "fine_tuned_model_name",  // Required: Fine-tuned model to use
    images: ["base64_or_url"],       // Optional: Images for multimodal models
    videos: ["base64_or_url"],       // Optional: Videos for multimodal models
    batch: false,                    // Default: false (process synchronously)
    config: {
      // Configuration options
    }
  }
}
```

## System Information

### `health_v1_health_get`
Health check endpoint.

### `get_models_v1_models_get`
Get the list of supported models.

### `get_domains_v1_domains_get`
Get the list of supported domains.

### `get_schema_v1_schema_post`
Get the JSON schema for a given domain.
```
{
  requestBody: {
    domain: "document.invoice",  // Required: Domain identifier
    gql_stmt: null               // Optional: GraphQL statement
  }
}
```

### `get_predictions_v1_predictions_get`
Get all predictions uploaded by the user with pagination.
```
{
  queryParameters: {
    skip: 0,      // Number of items to skip
    limit: 10     // Maximum number of items to return
  }
}
```

### `get_prediction_v1_predictions_id_get`
Get prediction JSON by request ID.
```
{
  urlParameters: {
    id: "prediction_id_here"  // Required: ID of the prediction to retrieve
  }
}
```

## Usage Notes

- Most functions require authentication, which should be handled by your client implementation
- For file uploads, you'll need to include the appropriate file data in the request body
- When processing media or documents, you can choose between synchronous (batch: false) and asynchronous (batch: true) processing
- Fine-tuning jobs may take significant time to complete; use the job ID to check status periodically

# Blood Test Analyzer

A servlet that analyzes blood test results and provides structured analysis with insights.

## Features

- Parses blood test data
- Categorizes test results
- Identifies abnormal values
- Generates health insights
- Provides recommendations

## Usage

Call with:

```json
{
  "params": {
    "name": "analyze_blood_test",
    "arguments": {
      "content": "blood test content here"
    }
  }
}
```

Returns:
```json
{
  "patientInfo": {
    "name": "string",
    "dateOfBirth": "string",
    "testDate": "string"
  },
  "categories": {
    "category_name": [
      {
        "name": "string",
        "value": "number",
        "unit": "string",
        "ref": "string",
        "status": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "insights": {
    "critical_markers": ["string"],
    "recommendations": ["string"]
  }
}

# Rigetti QCS API via MCP

A servlet for interacting with Rigetti's Quantum Cloud Services (QCS) API. This
servlet provides tools for managing quantum processors, reservations, and user
accounts.

## Configuration

Required configuration:

- `JWT_TOKEN`: API access token from
  [QCS Auth Token page](https://qcs.rigetti.com/auth/token)

## Tools

### Quantum Processor Management

#### List Quantum Processors (`list_quantum_processors`)

Lists all available quantum processors with pagination support.

```json
{
  "params": {
    "name": "list_quantum_processors",
    "arguments": {
      "queryParameters": {
        "pageSize": 5,
        "pageToken": "optional-pagination-token"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

#### Get Quantum Processor (`get_quantum_processor`)

Retrieves details about a specific quantum processor.

```json
{
  "params": {
    "name": "get_quantum_processor",
    "arguments": {
      "urlParameters": {
        "quantumProcessorId": "Aspen-M-3"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

#### Get Instruction Set Architecture (`get_instruction_set_architecture`)

Retrieves the ISA for a specific quantum processor.

```json
{
  "params": {
    "name": "get_instruction_set_architecture",
    "arguments": {
      "urlParameters": {
        "quantumProcessorId": "Aspen-M-3"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Reservation Management

#### Create Reservation (`create_reservation`)

Creates a new quantum processor reservation.

```json
{
  "params": {
    "name": "create_reservation",
    "arguments": {
      "requestBody": {
        "quantumProcessorId": "Aspen-M-3",
        "startTime": "2024-01-25T15:00:00Z",
        "endTime": "2024-01-25T16:00:00Z",
        "notes": "Running quantum error correction experiments",
        "accountType": "user"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

#### Find Available Reservations (`find_available_reservations`)

Lists currently available reservations on a quantum processor.

```json
{
  "params": {
    "name": "find_available_reservations",
    "arguments": {
      "queryParameters": {
        "quantumProcessorId": "Aspen-M-3",
        "startTimeFrom": "2024-01-24T00:00:00Z",
        "duration": "1h"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

#### List Reservations (`list_reservations`)

Lists reservations for the authenticated user. Supports filtering and sorting.

Filter fields:

- `startTime`
- `endTime`
- `createdTime`
- `price`
- `quantumProcessorId`

Sort fields:

- `startTime`
- `endTime`
- `createdTime`
- `price`

### Quantum Program Execution

#### Get Quilt Calibrations (`get_quilt_calibrations`)

Retrieves calibration data for client-side Quilt generation.

```json
{
  "params": {
    "name": "get_quilt_calibrations",
    "arguments": {
      "urlParameters": {
        "quantumProcessorId": "Aspen-M-3"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

#### Translate Native Quil (`translate_native_quil_to_encrypted_binary`)

Compiles Quil code to encrypted binary form for execution.

```json
{
  "params": {
    "name": "translate_native_quil_to_encrypted_binary",
    "arguments": {
      "urlParameters": {
        "quantumProcessorId": "Aspen-M-3"
      },
      "requestBody": {
        "quil": "DECLARE ro BIT[1]\nH 0\nMEASURE 0 ro[0]",
        "numShots": 1000
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### User & Group Management

#### Activate User (`activate_user`)

Completes user activation after invitation.

```json
{
  "params": {
    "name": "activate_user",
    "arguments": {
      "requestBody": {
        "profile": {
          "email": "researcher@university.edu",
          "firstName": "Jane",
          "lastName": "Doe",
          "organization": "Quantum Research Lab"
        },
        "credentials": {
          "password": {
            "value": "secure-password-here"
          }
        },
        "token": "verification-token-from-email"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

#### List Group Users (`list_group_users`)

Lists users in a group.

```json
{
  "params": {
    "name": "list_group_users",
    "arguments": {
      "urlParameters": {
        "groupName": "quantum-research-team"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Client Applications

#### List Client Applications (`list_client_applications`)

Lists supported Rigetti system components with version information. No
parameters required.

#### Get Client Application (`get_client_application`)

Gets details about a specific system component.

```json
{
  "params": {
    "name": "get_client_application",
    "arguments": {
      "urlParameters": {
        "clientApplicationName": "pyquil"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### System Status

#### List Viewer Announcements (`list_viewer_announcements`)

Lists system announcements for the authenticated user.

```json
{
  "params": {
    "name": "list_viewer_announcements",
    "arguments": {
      "queryParameters": {
        "includeDismissed": false
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Authentication

All requests require a valid OAuth2 Bearer token provided in the JWT_TOKEN
configuration. Tokens expire after 24 hours.

## Error Handling

The servlet returns errors in a standardized format:

```json
{
  "content": [{
    "type": "text",
    "text": "Error description"
  }],
  "isError": true
}
```
